          "path": "_m/g/c/3/d/newcastle-west-wp/fuller-s-folly-newcastle-west-.jpg",
          "filename": "Fuller's Folly, Newcastle West, Co. Limerick - geograph.org.uk - 372446.jpg",
          "caption": "Fuller's Folly, Newcastle West, Co. Limerick Fullers Folly is located south-east of the Desmond Castle. The man behind the construction of Fullers Folly was William Fuller Hartnett born in 1804. It is believed that Fuller had a disagreement with the Castle Authorities and as a result built this castle as a form of revenge or a hint to them. It was a costly structure with little or no use, hence 'Folly'. Fuller died in 1879, and was buried in Churchtown graveyard.",
          "alt": "Fuller's Folly, Newcastle West, Co. Limerick Fullers Folly is located south-east of the Desmond Castle. The man behind the construction of Fullers Folly was William Fuller Hartnett born in 1804. It is believed that Fuller had a disagreement with the Castle Authorities and as a result built this castle as a form of revenge or a hint to them. It was a costly structure with little or no use, hence 'Folly'. Fuller died in 1879, and was buried in Churchtown graveyard.",
